{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20422",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.66,
      "end_seconds": 2.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Evening. Let's get started."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.51,
      "end_seconds": 7.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "afternoon uh is this seat fine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 9.15,
      "end_seconds": 14.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Doctor I've come along because I know the history if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.5,
      "end_seconds": 19.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "So, start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.23,
      "end_seconds": 23.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "it's a dry cough, mostly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.39,
      "end_seconds": 27.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.2,
      "end_seconds": 43.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "It's been like this since last night. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.14,
      "end_seconds": 53.53,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.02,
      "end_seconds": 78.72,
      "duration_seconds": 22.7,
      "text": "Well, I'd say a couple of times a week. Only honey, and it's not much. It's mild, honestly. There's aching all over as well. About aching all over, I'd give it a eight, out of ten. Oh, and loss of taste."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.87,
      "end_seconds": 88.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.53,
      "end_seconds": 92.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "my mother had a stroke"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.07,
      "end_seconds": 113.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.62,
      "end_seconds": 127.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.03,
      "text": "hmm there was some antibiotic I was told I was allergic but I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.39,
      "end_seconds": 130.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 131.48,
      "end_seconds": 135.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "yes I had my septum straightened in my thirties"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.57,
      "end_seconds": 140.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.23,
      "end_seconds": 147.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "I have diabetes for two years. High blood pressure for two years"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.2,
      "end_seconds": 154.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "yes alright, diabetes, that matches what I have here do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 158.02,
      "end_seconds": 162.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.96,
      "end_seconds": 164.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.67,
      "end_seconds": 168.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "I only drink at family occasions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.52,
      "end_seconds": 170.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.3,
      "text": "are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.41,
      "end_seconds": 174.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.23,
      "end_seconds": 179.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Are you in work at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.24,
      "end_seconds": 184.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.7,
      "end_seconds": 187.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "do you live by yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.43,
      "end_seconds": 193.46,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "No, I share a house with my brother."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.5,
      "end_seconds": 198.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.69,
      "end_seconds": 202.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "mm, it's gliclazide, 80 milligrams, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 204.64,
      "end_seconds": 214.85,
      "duration_seconds": 10.21,
      "text": "sorry what was I saying doctor I think the last prescription for the gliclazide was 40 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.39,
      "end_seconds": 220.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.89,
      "end_seconds": 243.06,
      "duration_seconds": 21.17,
      "text": "I don't think I have it with me. It's telmisartan 40 milligrams once a day. I told my wife I'd come today. I did try to ignore it for a while. Dolo 650 milligrams when I get the fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.76,
      "end_seconds": 249.39,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "let me check a few things any leg swelling confusion vomiting or diarrhoea?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.24,
      "end_seconds": 254.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Actually, no, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.25,
      "end_seconds": 264.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "have you had any blue lips or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.58,
      "end_seconds": 269.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "no blue lips or chest pain, none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.14,
      "end_seconds": 275.58,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "any pins and needles or loss of strength anywhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.31,
      "end_seconds": 278.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.19,
      "end_seconds": 283.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.47,
      "end_seconds": 286.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.0,
      "text": "no rashes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.88,
      "end_seconds": 292.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "now I'm going to do a short physical check"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.55,
      "end_seconds": 294.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.13,
      "text": "Sure thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.04,
      "end_seconds": 297.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.11,
      "end_seconds": 313.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "your chest is clear apart from a few crackles at the right base and your oxygen level is a bit low"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.08,
      "end_seconds": 319.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.27,
      "end_seconds": 361.72,
      "duration_seconds": 24.45,
      "text": "okay thinking it through I don't have a clear answer today: a viral chest infection with mildly low oxygen is possible and so is a bacterial pneumonia. I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray for low oxygen and crackles. I'll request a viral swab it'll help with fever and cough"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.64,
      "end_seconds": 364.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Okay I'll do it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.62,
      "end_seconds": 384.3,
      "duration_seconds": 17.68,
      "text": "rest, keep your fluids up and lie on your tummy or side to help your breathing. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.82,
      "end_seconds": 389.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "yes I'll bear that that in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.64,
      "end_seconds": 404.0,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: you become more breathless or confused. In that case don't wait. Let's review you after the chest X-ray. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.83,
      "end_seconds": 409.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 413.45,
      "end_seconds": 415.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "So, all the best."
    }
  ]
}